 Client Collector installation on a Linux OS system","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/agent-client-collector/acc-install-linux-concept.md","line":184},{"title":"Install the Agent Client Collector on a Windows machine manually","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/agent-client-collector/acc-install-windows.md","line":186},{"title":"Agent Client Collector installation on a macOS system","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/agent-client-collector/acc-install-mac-os.md","line":188},{"title":"Agent Client Collector","target":"acc-landing-page","line":192},{"title":"MID Web Server","target":"mid-web-server","line":193}],"metadata":{"title":"Agent Client Collector installation","description":"You can install the Agent Client Collector on any supported host machine. The Agent Client Collector connects to a MID Server using the HTTP/S protocol, and the connection remains active after being established. One MID Server may handle several agents simultaneously, while a single agent works with one MID Server at a time and switches to a different MID Server when necessary to provide failover protection.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-operations-management/agent-client-collector/acc-installation.html","release":"australia","product":"Agent Client Collector","classification":"agent-client-collector","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":3,"breadcrumb":["ACC deployment - servers","Configuring Agent Client Collector","Agent Client Collector","IT Operations Management"],"tags":["#it-operations-management","#acc","#agent","#endpoint","#monitoring","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/it-operations-management/agent-client-collector/acc-installation.md"},
